<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bai Bureh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1840–<a href="/years/1908">1908</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bai Bureh was a Temne ruler and war leader in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> who led the Hut Tax War of 1898 against British rule. Opposing the new tax on dwellings in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, his fighters waged a skilled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> campaign for months before he surrendered. The British exiled him to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>, but he was allowed to return in 1905 and is now a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bai-bureh.jpg" alt="Bai Bureh" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lieutenant Arthur Greer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bai_Bureh_(1898).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
